# Overview
#
# A wordy phrase is a stock phrase that has a shorter form (`prior to`
# for `before`, `the majority of` for `most`). The reader reads several
# words for the meaning of one. Each phrase in this rule has a one-word
# equivalent (`because`, `before`, `can`, `about`, `most`, `many`,
# `few`, `enough`, `first`, `whether`, `similarly`, `for`, `to`), and
# the fix writes it. The rule sits at Required, because it matches exact
# phrases and the fix is mechanical.
#
# Expression
#
# `main` lists each phrase. `be able to` counts only after `is`, `are`,
# `was`, `were`, or `will`, where `can` or `could` replaces it.
#
# False Positives
#
# `whether or not` is left out, because its common sense in docs is
# `regardless of whether` (`renders the path whether or not the binding
# has a location`), and `whether` alone does not carry that sense. After
# `must` or `should`, `be able to` has no short form (`the caller must
# be able to cancel`), so it passes there. `at the same time as` stays
# out, because its one-word form `while` also reads as a contrast.
#
# Related Rules
#
# ProseInOrderTo reports `in order to`, and ProseDueToTheFact reports
# `due to the fact that`, each with a rewrite. The Required
# ProseRedundantPair reports `close proximity`. None of them repeats
# here as a second finding on the same words.
#
# The Recommended ProseWordy holds `a number of`, `in terms of`, and the
# other phrases that also have a literal sense, which the short form
# does not carry. The Required ProseWordy holds every other wordy
# phrase.
#
# Measurement
#
# The rule hit 322 lines in the measure.py corpus, and 20 of 20 sampled
# hits had a shorter form.
expr main [
    (owing to the fact that),
    (at this point in time),
    (at the present time),
    (for the purpose of),
    (in the process of),
    (is able to),
    (are able to),
    (was able to),
    (were able to),
    (will be able to),
    (has the ability to),
    (have the ability to),
    (in spite of the fact that),
    (despite the fact that),
    (with regard to),
    (with regards to),
    (in regards to),
    (in regard to),
    (the majority of),
    (a majority of),
    (prior to),
    (subsequent to),
    (in the case of),
    (in cases where),
    (in the case where),
    (in the event of),
    (in the event that),
    (it is possible to),
    (it is possible for),
    (as a result of),
    (for the reason that),
    (on the basis of),
    (in the absence of),
    (so as to),
    (in order for),
    (in the near future),
    (on a regular basis),
    (on a daily basis),
    (in a timely manner),
    (in an effort to),
    (in the course of),
    (with the exception of),
    (at all times),
    (until such time as),
    (in conjunction with),
    (in accordance with),
    (a large number of),
    (a small number of),
    (the vast majority of),
    (in excess of),
    (upwards of),
    (as to whether),
    (for all intents and purposes),
    (first of all),
    (last but not least),
    (in and of itself),
    (with reference to),
    (in reference to),
    (pertaining to),
    (on account of),
    (by virtue of),
    (during the course of),
    (a sufficient number of),
    (in a similar way),
    (in a similar manner),
    (in a similar fashion),
    (for the sake of),
    (with the aim of)
]
let message "Wordy. Use the short form."
let description "Flags stock phrases with a one-word equivalent."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The path renders whether or not the binding has a location."
allows "The scheduler retries the job because the lease expired."
allows "Close the file before the next read."
allows "The caller must be able to cancel the request."
